---
layout: base.njk
title: Markets today
permalink: /dashboards/markets/
description: "A US-led market dashboard: the Magnificent 7 and top US and UK stocks, today's movers, what market news is talking about, Treasury yields and the week's big economic events."
---
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="eyebrow">Dashboard · Markets</div>
  <h1>Markets today</h1>
  <p class="lede">The Magnificent 7, the biggest US and UK names and what moved today, alongside {{ markets.headlineCount | num }} market headlines from the last two days and the US Treasury yield curve.</p>
</div>

<div class="tv-widget tv-tape" data-widget="ticker-tape" data-config-src="tv-tape"><p class="muted">Loading market prices…</p></div>

{# ---------- Prices: TradingView widgets (delayed quotes, licensed for embedding) ---------- #}
<section>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>The Magnificent 7</h2>
    <p class="muted">Three months of price for each. Pick a tab to switch company. Prices are delayed about 15 minutes.</p>
    <div class="tv-widget" data-widget="symbol-overview" data-config-src="tv-mag7" data-height="420"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="grid two">
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Watchlist</h2>
    <p class="muted">Today's price and change: Magnificent 7, more US leaders and the FTSE 100's biggest names. Delayed about 15 minutes.</p>
    <div class="tv-widget" data-widget="market-quotes" data-config-src="tv-quotes" data-height="520"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Today's US movers</h2>
    <p class="muted">Biggest gainers, losers and most active US stocks.</p>
    <div class="tv-widget" data-widget="hotlists" data-config-src="tv-movers" data-height="520"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>The S&amp;P 500 at a glance</h2>
    <p class="muted">Each block is a company, sized by market value and coloured by today's move. The Magnificent 7 are the biggest blocks.</p>
    <div class="tv-widget tv-heatmap" data-widget="stock-heatmap" data-config-src="tv-heatmap" data-height="520"></div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- News: built here from RSS ---------- #}
{% set th = { label: 'Market headlines by theme', unit: 'headlines', rows: [] } %}
{% for t in markets.themes %}{% if t.count %}{% set th = (th.rows.push({ label: t.name, value: t.count }), th) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% set m7 = { label: 'Magnificent 7 mentions in market headlines', unit: 'headlines', rows: [] } %}
{% for t in markets.mag7 %}{% set m7 = (m7.rows.push({ label: t.name, value: t.count }), m7) %}{% endfor %}

<section>
  <div class="page-head" style="padding-top:16px">
    <div class="eyebrow">News · last 48 hours</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">What the market is talking about</h2>
    <p class="muted">{{ markets.headlineCount | num }} headlines from {% for s in markets.sources %}{{ s.name }}{% if not loop.last %}{{ ' and ' if loop.revindex0 == 1 else ', ' }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}, sorted into themes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="card chart-card">
      <h2>Themes in the headlines</h2>
      <p class="muted">Headlines mentioning each theme. One headline can count towards several.</p>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="bar" data-src="themes-data"></div>
      <details class="table"><summary>View as table</summary><div class="tablewrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Theme</th><th>Headlines</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for t in markets.themes %}<tr><td>{{ t.name }}</td><td>{{ t.count }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="card chart-card">
      <h2>Magnificent 7 in the news</h2>
      <p class="muted">Headlines naming each company, its ticker or its best-known products.</p>
      <div class="chart" data-chart="bar" data-src="mag7-data"></div>
      <details class="table"><summary>View as table</summary><div class="tablewrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Headlines</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for t in markets.mag7 %}<tr><td>{{ t.name }}</td><td>{{ t.count }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Latest market headlines</h2>
    <ul class="storylist">
      {% for s in markets.latest %}
      <li><a href="{{ s.link }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">{{ s.title }}</a><div class="meta">{{ s.source }} · {{ s.date | ago }}</div></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Rates: US Treasury (public domain) ---------- #}
{% if markets.yields %}
{% set y = markets.yields %}
{% set yc = { label: 'US Treasury yields, last three months', unit: '%', yMin: y.chartFloor or 0, series: [
  { label: '2-year', slot: 1, points: [] }, { label: '10-year', slot: 2, points: [] }, { label: '30-year', slot: 3, points: [] } ] } %}
{% for r in y.history %}{% if r.y2 != null and r.y30 != null %}
  {% set _ = yc.series[0].points.push({ date: r.date, value: r.y2 }) %}{% set _ = yc.series[1].points.push({ date: r.date, value: r.y10 }) %}{% set _ = yc.series[2].points.push({ date: r.date, value: r.y30 }) %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
<section>
  <div class="page-head" style="padding-top:16px">
    <div class="eyebrow">Rates · US Treasury</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem">The price of money</h2>
    <p class="muted">Treasury yields set the cost of borrowing across the economy. Rising yields usually weigh on share prices, especially tech.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid three">
    {% for k in [['y2', '2-year', 1], ['y10', '10-year', 2], ['y30', '30-year', 3]] %}
    {% set now = y.latest[k[0]] %}{% set was = y.monthAgo[k[0]] %}{% set diff = ((now - was) * 100) | round %}
    <div class="card stat tint-{{ k[2] }} reveal">
      <div class="value">{{ now.toFixed(2) }}%</div>
      <div class="label">{{ k[1] }} yield · {% if diff > 0 %}up {{ diff }}{% elif diff < 0 %}down {{ -diff }}{% else %}unchanged,{% endif %}{% if diff != 0 %} basis points{% endif %} in a month</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="card chart-card" style="margin-top:16px">
    <h2>Yields over three months</h2>
    <p class="muted">Daily closing yield. Hover for values.</p>
    <div class="chart" data-chart="line" data-src="yields-data"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Source: <a href="https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates" rel="noopener">US Department of the Treasury</a>, as of {{ y.latest.date }}.</p>
</section>
<script type="application/json" id="yields-data">{{ yc | json | safe }}</script>
{% endif %}

<section>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Coming up</h2>
    <p class="muted">The US and UK economic releases and central bank decisions that move markets: rate decisions, inflation and jobs data.</p>
    <div class="tv-widget" data-widget="events" data-config-src="tv-events" data-height="520"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted disclaimer"><b>Not financial advice.</b> Stock and index prices are delayed about 15 minutes (a <b>D</b> next to a price marks it as delayed) and come from <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/" rel="noopener">TradingView</a>; headlines link to their publishers; nothing here is a recommendation to buy or sell. See the <a href="/terms/">terms and disclaimer</a>. News updated {{ markets.updated | when }}.</p>
</section>

<script type="application/json" id="themes-data">{{ th | json | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="mag7-data">{{ m7 | json | safe }}</script>

{# Widget configs. Symbols use TradingView's names; FOREXCOM/OANDA CFDs stand in for indices, which exchanges don't licence for free embeds. #}
